          "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Mn6Ge2 (reduced formula Mn3Ge) crystallizes in the hexagonal space group P6_3/mmc (No. 194), with 8 atoms per unit cell distributed over 2 independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows both Ge and Mn centers adopt close-packed-like local arrangements with 12 geometric neighbors each: Ge is surrounded by 12 Mn neighbors (2.6109–2.65 Å), while Mn has 4 Ge and 8 Mn neighbors (2.6109–2.7186 Å). The periodic neighbor graph forms a single 3-dimensional component spanning all 8 sites, and validated polyhedron contacts reveal Mn–Mn 12-vertex polyhedra sharing corners, edges, and faces, alongside corner- and edge-sharing between Ge and Mn polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
